$f(x)=\cos 2 x+x$ on $\left[-\frac{\pi}{2}, \frac{\pi}{2}\right]$
Find the value of $f(x)$ at boundary of interval i.e at $\mathrm{x}=\frac{-\pi}{2}$ and $\mathrm{x}=\frac{\pi}{2}\begin{aligned}
& f\left(\frac{-\pi}{2}\right)=-1+\frac{-\pi}{2} \\
& f\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)=-1+\frac{\pi}{2}
\end{aligned}$
So, minimum value of $\mathrm{f}(\mathrm{x})^2=-\left(1+\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$
